{
  "format": "simple-touch-manual/3",
  "firmware": {
    "name": "TouchVink",
    "author": "Jon Waterschoot",
    "version": "0.2",
    "description": "A feedback instrument after the self-regulating tape / ring-mod / reverb patches of Jaap Vink. One knob, one function.",
    "notes": "## TouchVink\nSource: [jonwaterschoot/TouchVink](https://github.com/jonwaterschoot/TouchVink). Interactive manual: [jonwaterschoot.github.io/TouchVink](https://jonwaterschoot.github.io/TouchVink/).\n\nA delayed copy of the output is ring-modulated, reverberated and passed through a VCA that the loop's own loudness turns down, so the loop can run above unity gain and keep moving by itself.\n\n## Pads\n- **P00** · pads to OSC mode: P03–P09 pick the oscillator pitch and excite the loop; pressure bends up to an octave\n- **P02** · pads to DIST mode: P03–P09 pick the distortion; pressure adds drive\n- **P01** · steering: loop swells re-pick the oscillator pitch. Tap on / off, hold for momentary\n- **P10** · attack 2 ms / 60 ms / 600 ms\n- **P11** · decay, tap: 120 ms / 2 s / drone; hold ½ s: back to 120 ms\n- **P10 + P11**, hold 1 s · recalibrate the pads\n\n## Switches\n- **S09-S10** · osc motion: LFO sweep / steady / drunk walk\n- **S07-S08** · noise: pink / drift / brown\n\n## MIDI\n- ch 1 notes · oscillator pitch + excite\n- ch 10 notes 36–47 · pads P0–P11\n- CC 20–27 · S30–S37\n- CC 28–34 · SW1, SW2, pad mode, attack, decay, steer, distortion",
    "repo": "https://github.com/jonwaterschoot/TouchVink"
  },
